      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2><details class="ba-faq"><summary>How do I make Amla taste nicer?</summary><p>Try it in sparkling water with lime and mint, or blended into a fruit smoothie.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>What is Amla?</summary><p>Amla (Phyllanthus emblica), also called Indian gooseberry, is a round, pale-green, very sour fruit eaten fresh, pickled, dried and powdered across India.</p></details><details class="ba-faq"><summary>How much Vitamin C is in a serving of Amla powder?</summary><p>Our label lists 25 mg of Vitamin C per serving, which is 28% of the Daily Value.</p></details>
